{"id":"n-20261006-bj20ao","category":"tech","display_title":"Former PlayStation Boss Questions Discs","display_title_he":"בכיר פלייסטיישן לשעבר מטיל ספק בהורדת הדיסקים","short_summary":"Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden has criticized Sony's upcoming decision to eliminate physical discs, raising concerns about digital ownership and brand reputation.","english_level":"C1","words":414,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/if-you-cant-own-it-what-are-you-buying-former-playstation-boss-questions-sonys-decision-to-kill-discs","title":"\"If You Can't Own It, What Are You Buying?\" – Former PlayStation Boss Questions Sony's Decision to Kill Discs","published_at":"2026-10-06T14:53:56.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-06T14:53:56.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-06T16:08:54.958Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The gaming industry has faced significant backlash following Sony's announcement that it will completely phase out PlayStation physical discs beginning in 2028. Weighing in on the controversy, former PlayStation executive Shawn Layden recently discussed the dramatic shift during an appearance on The Expansion Pass podcast.","While Layden was not part of the internal discussions when the strategy was formulated, he acknowledged the undeniable appeal of digital convenience. He remarked that downloading a game is preferred by many not just because it avoids trips to a retail store, but because it removes the minor effort of placing a disc into a console from across the living room. Nevertheless, Layden argued that abandoning physical media entirely is a misguided strategy.","According to Layden, although digital downloads likely account for roughly eighty percent of the market, the remaining twenty percent represents the most devoted segment of the consumer base. This faithful group often purchases multiple physical copies, including unopened collector editions preserved in their original packaging, with one copy never even leaving the shrink wrap. Beyond collecting habits, Layden emphasized that the core problem involves consumer ownership rights. Drawing a parallel to the personal computer market, where platforms like Steam have dominated for years, he noted that players on PC at least have alternatives like GOG, which often allows users to download games without DRM and archive them on personal discs. PlayStation, however, will likely never offer that option.","Layden explained that if a consumer cannot legally resell an item, they do not truly own it, meaning purchasers are merely buying digital access rather than tangible assets. He noted that buying access does not sound particularly appealing. He warned that this distinction diminishes the perceived value of purchases and fuels consumer anxiety, particularly when buyers witness companies revoking access to previously acquired digital media like movies. Consequently, Layden believes these fears expose Sony to severe reputational damage and brand harm, as consumers naturally game out the worst-case scenario. This backlash represents a huge hit to Sony's reputation, leaving many to wonder whether the financial savings achieved by halting disc production will truly be worth the ill will generated among loyal gamers.","In addition to the physical media controversy, Sony has recently explored other contentious developments, including patent applications for artificial intelligence patches designed to adjust console performance with vibe-coded fixes and integrated near-field communication readers within controllers. Observers note that only time will reveal whether the cost reductions of going entirely digital will justify the widespread dissatisfaction generated."],"facts":[{"fact":"Shawn Layden, the former PlayStation boss, questioned Sony's decision to eliminate PlayStation discs starting in 2028 during an interview on The Expansion Pass podcast.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Layden acknowledged that while digital downloads offer convenience, completely removing discs alienates a dedicated 20% minority of faithful consumers who collect physical media.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"He raised concerns about consumer ownership, stating that if buyers cannot sell a game, they merely purchase temporary access rather than true property.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Layden noted that Sony's decision harms its brand reputation, exacerbated by consumer fears of losing access to purchased digital libraries, similar to previous movie revocations.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"gaming","lemma":"gaming","pos":"noun","he":"משחקי מחשב / גיימינג","name":false},{"text":"industry","lemma":"industry","pos":"noun","he":"תעשייה","name":false},{"text":"faced","lemma":"face","pos":"verb","he":"התמודד עם","name":false},{"text":"significant","lemma":"significant","pos":"adjective","he":"משמעותי","name":false},{"text":"backlash","lemma":"backlash","pos":"noun","he":"תגובת נגד","name":false},{"text":"following","lemma":"follow","pos":"preposition","he":"בעקבות","name":false},{"text":"announcement","lemma":"announcement","pos":"noun","he":"הודעה","name":false},{"text":"completely","lemma":"completely","pos":"adverb","he":"לחלוטין","name":false},{"text":"phase out","lemma":"phase out","pos":"verb","he":"להפסיק בהדרגה","name":false},{"text":"physical","lemma":"physical","pos":"adjective","he":"פיזי","name":false},{"text":"discs","lemma":"disc","pos":"noun","he":"תקליטורים / דיסקים","name":false},{"text":"beginning","lemma":"begin","pos":"verb","he":"להתחיל","name":false},{"text":"weighing in","lemma":"weigh in","pos":"verb","he":"להביע דעה / להתערב","name":false},{"text":"controversy","lemma":"controversy","pos":"noun","he":"מחלוקת","name":false},{"text":"executive","lemma":"executive","pos":"noun","he":"מנהל בכיר","name":false},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"adverb","he":"לאחרונה","name":false},{"te